From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2_codec2: advertise VP9 levels 5.1 and 5.2 by default

When no decoder device lists the codec's input format, or a device's
level control yields no recognised level, DecodeInterface falls back to
a fixed list of levels per codec. For VP9 that list ends at level 5,
whose luma sample rate allows 3840x2160 at about 37 frames per second.
Players check a stream's level against the decoder's profile levels, so
with this list a 4K60 VP9 stream (level 5.1, as served for example by
YouTube) would be treated as beyond the hardware decoder's capabilities,
and Media3 would prefer the software decoder.

Add levels 5.1 and 5.2 (3840x2160 up to about 141 frames per second), so
that this list matches the fallback list of V4L2Device::queryC2Levels(),
which the following patch extends in the same way. The decoder's size
and rate limits in the media codecs XML still bound what is advertised.

The hardware sustains these levels: on SC8280XP (Huawei MateBook E Go),
3840x2160 VP9 at 120 fps and 100 Mbit/s decoded in real time for 30 s
with no frame late by more than a frame period.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 components/DecodeInterface.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/DecodeInterface.cpp b/components/DecodeInterface.cpp
index 17fce34..0ffedd8 100644
--- a/components/DecodeInterface.cpp
+++ b/components/DecodeInterface.cpp
@@ -227,7 +227,8 @@ DecodeInterface::DecodeInterface(const std::string& name,
         case VideoCodec::VP9:
             levels = {C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_1,   C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_1_1, C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_2,
                       C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_2_1, C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_3,   C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_3_1,
-                      C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_4,   C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_4_1, C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_5};
+                      C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_4,   C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_4_1, C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_5,
+                      C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_5_1, C2Config::LEVEL_VP9_5_2};
             break;
         case VideoCodec::HEVC:
             levels = {C2Config::LEVEL_HEVC_MAIN_1,   C2Config::LEVEL_HEVC_MAIN_2,
